P10 (issue #23, U20): fill the static table of the 16-items machine
before the threads start.

m16_create fills the static table hibit[] on first use, testing
hibit[0] != 0 as "not yet filled" and writing hibit[0] = 0 first. When
two threads create their first machine at the same time, the second one
sees hibit[0] == 0 and uses the partly filled table: a data race that
makes multi-threaded runs with the 16-items machine (-As, -Ad, -l > 0,
-Z > 1) nondeterministic (14 of 400 runs of one command under load gave
7 different spectra). Creating and deleting one machine in fpg_genpsp,
before any thread, fills the table once.

--- a/fpgrowth/src/fpgpsp.c
+++ b/fpgrowth/src/fpgpsp.c
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@
 #endif
 #include "patspec.h"
 #include "fpgpsp.h"
+#include "fim16.h"              /* P10 */
 #ifdef FPGPSP_MAIN
 #include "error.h"
 #endif
@@ -268,6 +269,7 @@
   if (seed == 0) seed = (long)time(NULL);
   if (surr == FPG_SHUFFLE)      /* P9: no 16-items machine for */
     mode &= ~FPG_FIM16;         /* unrecoded data */
+  m16_delete(m16_create(+1, 1, NULL)); /* P10: fill the static table */
 
   /* --- prepare data --- */
   fpgrowth = fpg_create(target, supp, 100.0, 100.0, zmin, zmax,
